    recordTitle: "Making clips by recording",
    recordLead: "The easiest way to make a clip is to <strong>record</strong> it in Unity's Animation window. While recording, any value you change in the Inspector is written into the clip. Here you'll make <code>Hat_ON</code>, a clip that shows the hat, and <code>Hat_OFF</code>, a clip that hides it. Assume the hat (Hat) is a child of Accessories in the avatar, and is normally turned off.",
    prepTitle: "Preparation: make the clips and the controller",
    prep: [
      "Make a folder for the gimmick in the Project window. Right-click inside <code>Assets</code>, choose <code>Create → Folder</code>, and give it a name (for example, <code>Hat</code> inside <code>MyGimmicks</code>). Keeping each gimmick in its own folder makes things easier to find later.",
      "Right-click inside that folder, choose <code>Create → Animation</code>, and name it <code>Hat_ON</code>. Make <code>Hat_OFF</code> the same way. In some Unity versions, it's at <code>Create → Animation → Animation Clip</code>.",
      "Right-click in the same folder, choose <code>Create → Animator Controller</code>, and name it <code>Hat_FX</code>.",
      "Double-click <code>Hat_FX</code> to open it in the Animator window. Drag the <code>Hat_OFF</code> and <code>Hat_ON</code> files into the graph. This makes two states with the clips in them. The Animation window only lets you pick clips that are in the selected Animator's controller, so turn them into states first.",
      "In the Hierarchy, select the top object of your avatar (the one with the VRC Avatar Descriptor). Drag <code>Hat_FX</code> into the <code>Controller</code> field of the Animator component in the Inspector. <strong>This is only temporary, for recording.</strong>",
    ],
    stepsTitle: "Record",
    steps: [
      "Open the Animation window with <code>Window → Animation → Animation</code> (or press Ctrl + 6). Keep the top object of your avatar selected in the Hierarchy.",
