    keysTitle: "Keyframes and clip length",
    keys: [
      "A keyframe marks the value at a certain time. Between keys, Unity fills in the values smoothly. If you put a key of 0 at frame 0 and a key of 100 at frame 60, you get a clip that changes from 0 to 100 over 1 second (when 1 second is 60 frames).",
      "<strong>In an on/off clip, the value doesn't change.</strong> The hat stays out the whole time it's shown. So two keys with the same value, at frame 0 and frame 1, are enough. The length is almost 0, but as long as it's in the state, the Animator keeps writing this value.",
